  'This undergraduate Social Work elective introduces behavioral health systems, mental health and substance use concerns, DSM-informed language, trauma-informed care, crisis response, evidence-based treatment pathways, recovery, and coordinated supports through a person-in-environment and social justice lens.',
  $mhbhjson${"slug": "mental-health-behavioral-health", "title": "Mental Health / Behavioral Health", "description": "This undergraduate Social Work elective introduces behavioral health systems, mental health and substance use concerns, DSM-informed language, trauma-informed care, crisis response, evidence-based treatment pathways, recovery, and coordinated supports through a person-in-environment and social justice lens.", "topics": [{"id": "2417f29e-00c4-4be5-ac33-fea5ceb93617", "type": "topic", "title": "Behavioral Health Systems and the Social Work Role", "description": "Understand mental health systems, behavioral health service settings, and social work's person-in-environment role.", "children": [{"id": "582af6b0-9690-48bf-a3f7-34ab84659164", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral health system overview", "children": [{"id": "fe8ad43a-f77f-4826-a077-a1984ec11d57", "type": "concept", "title": "Community mental health centers"}, {"id": "5ecfe216-8338-4b69-a22c-9c13dd39717e", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary care and integrated care"}, {"id": "a07a2ee2-9138-4e03-9ce5-c39f5c9c4eb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Inpatient, outpatient, crisis, residential, and peer-led settings"}, {"id": "cff0304d-2749-45c3-bf3f-6dc36bf88c3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Access, insurance, waitlists, and service gaps"}], "description": "This subtopic orients students to the places where people seek help and the fragmented systems they often navigate."}, {"id": "b0822d0e-f128-4bbc-aee7-0fdcaf7ab6f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social work role and scope", "children": [{"id": "debf49fa-fb03-4b25-8457-4d9b09aeab41", "type": "concept", "title": "Case management and care coordination"}, {"id": "296c710f-5831-44fb-b98e-3ef610584c57", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical support and psychoeducation"}, {"id": "7d0a5d3d-64bb-42c2-9ae5-44e5edd972b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Advocacy and rights protection"}, {"id": "db944145-3dd3-46fa-b9bc-c28cc55bc830", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision, referral, and scope limits"}], "description": "Students learn what social workers contribute to behavioral health through assessment, advocacy, coordination, and person-in-environment practice."}, {"id": "34197df2-699e-42c8-9743-391de8a7f271", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Person-in-environment lens", "children": [{"id": "d3d72cbb-fd02-4357-a0e9-049b5fa7f050", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, school, work, housing, legal, and community context"}, {"id": "40ccdf73-4b39-46f8-9c97-ac035fdd8f8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths and protective factors"}, {"id": "2a6f3cca-a211-4d1f-ba08-dc812b2993dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Social determinants of mental health"}, {"id": "ca1fd9fa-07d8-4029-8e70-06062fa26f39", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental stressors and supports"}], "description": "The point is to connect symptoms to context without reducing people to diagnoses."}]}, {"id": "88c068a5-1530-41f9-8cc3-1c6ce7e6772b", "type": "topic", "title": "Stigma, Social Determinants, Equity, and Mental Health", "description": "Examine how structural inequity, stigma, culture, and social determinants shape behavioral health.", "children": [{"id": "abd6fa16-35ed-402f-a505-db439106c94a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stigma and public attitudes", "children": [{"id": "99a012f5-b720-4af0-9f4c-dea820b11e49", "type": "concept", "title": "Public stigma"}, {"id": "e26b9dce-1ff3-4c8d-bacb-30a8471f0079", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-stigma"}, {"id": "01726451-0b54-4108-9226-4c93959a2c45", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural stigma"}, {"id": "2066e18f-5f02-45dc-83af-e3070ef2854c", "type": "concept", "title": "Language and recovery-oriented framing"}], "description": "Stigma shapes whether people seek care, disclose concerns, or receive respectful services."}, {"id": "19820e48-ac76-46d7-a05e-9a21e7ee811b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social determinants of behavioral health", "children": [{"id": "3492194e-f16c-4b60-b2ee-58c05a371676", "type": "concept", "title": "Poverty, housing, food security, employment, education, and transportation"}, {"id": "591bb4d8-2807-48a8-b458-37c712fb8306", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure to violence and discrimination"}, {"id": "18b9f85c-0fe1-4f2c-aec0-ad8e628c7ccb", "type": "concept", "title": "Healthcare access"}, {"id": "0e148f6c-51d2-4867-b7be-e9896d9a6489", "type": "concept", "title": "Community connection and belonging"}], "description": "Students examine how social conditions influence risk, resilience, access, and outcomes."}, {"id": "a869aa99-edf4-4bbb-a481-1e422a9c3097", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity and anti-oppressive practice", "children": [{"id": "e95fa234-d3ec-4598-9d4d-d07503867665", "type": "concept", "title": "Diagnostic bias"}, {"id": "f08db079-cd2b-42c2-9403-64cef878fe5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Culturally responsive care"}, {"id": "7cf64728-fb75-4372-ab6a-db3ce46d3e21", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access"}, {"id": "c90a282a-2700-4550-beec-7d3cfcb63ec5", "type": "concept", "title": "Client-defined wellbeing"}], "description": "Behavioral health practice must account for racism, ableism, classism, heterosexism, transphobia, and other forms of oppression."}]}, {"id": "7f1c08c5-f9e8-471c-8ead-04c722cbf071", "type": "topic", "title": "DSM-5-TR and Diagnostic Systems for Social Work Learners", "description": "Learn diagnostic language, classification systems, and the limits of diagnosis in social work practice.", "children": [{"id": "234cd700-f8c8-40c3-b865-85533e961f79", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purpose of diagnostic systems", "children": [{"id": "4096f648-1e8c-414e-9508-e2c62c7ac65c", "type": "concept", "title": "DSM-5-TR structure"}, {"id": "4da9e281-1c1b-4d93-90e4-b219f3e323b3", "type": "concept", "title": "ICD links"}, {"id": "3bc6aed9-b1be-47eb-b03a-5a63c273da34", "type": "concept", "title": "Diagnosis and access to services"}, {"id": "20a33d7a-d16b-435b-b0df-d8b49f2d1636", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits and risks of labels"}], "description": "Students learn why diagnostic systems exist and how they are used in services, billing, communication, and research."}, {"id": "307dad05-a1e8-4535-bdf8-7efaa150d270", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using diagnosis carefully", "children": [{"id": "8a573e77-4516-4f28-ac70-a6718d3217b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Symptoms versus diagnoses"}, {"id": "ce624631-1a70-4206-ad8a-ba4a35661eb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical significance and impairment"}, {"id": "de18954a-406d-4560-a7c5-b6e51ceab028", "type": "concept", "title": "Provisional thinking"}, {"id": "10ecebbf-ac37-41bf-9f1c-ba5262b39e21", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral and supervision"}], "description": "The goal is diagnostic literacy, not overconfidence. Students learn to distinguish undergraduate familiarity from licensed diagnostic authority."}, {"id": "93c9a8d1-5299-41ab-b3d0-0079a4bfa822", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Limits and critiques", "children": [{"id": "b6b00c2d-2d77-4821-9c0e-a91a8071daf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural formulation"}, {"id": "f5dac5d3-c059-4c64-8366-bdb7972a68a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicalization concerns"}, {"id": "0899c113-df3a-469c-afb4-1ef793abc801", "type": "concept", "title": "Social suffering and structural conditions"}, {"id": "b807afda-3858-427b-b1cd-5556cf7247db", "type": "concept", "title": "Client voice and meaning"}], "description": "Diagnosis should be used with awareness of culture, power, and context."}]}, {"id": "15b0e639-11a5-4eb6-b34b-3ad423100367", "type": "topic", "title": "Engagement, Helping Relationships, and Basic Interviewing", "description": "Practice respectful engagement, rapport, interviewing, and client-centered communication.", "children": [{"id": "1280417f-5bd4-4b86-8b18-1785ae14f4d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement and rapport", "children": [{"id": "2b8c0846-70ac-46c2-80d6-72acdfb69ef1", "type": "concept", "title": "Warmth and empathy"}, {"id": "13dff9e6-d61e-40bc-8e8e-b0a5ad503587", "type": "concept", "title": "Role explanation"}, {"id": "2b569e7b-c9cd-4a30-bf9d-2c72d510dc18", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaborative agenda setting"}, {"id": "fe15fc6f-9e41-4f0c-a5c3-5e91474263cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with reluctance or mandated involvement"}], "description": "Behavioral health work starts with trust, clarity, and respect."}, {"id": "29a38e6c-5271-46e9-9c04-4d641c22c993", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Basic interviewing skills", "children": [{"id": "8fc439be-4eec-44a7-a70e-c42a13055ab2", "type": "concept", "title": "Open questions"}, {"id": "e165290c-a4ea-4160-9d40-15721b010aa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Affirmations and reflections"}, {"id": "716a633d-3c31-48ca-a3ab-287af7779eb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Summarizing"}, {"id": "23b6123d-d1c6-4aed-be2b-ec3a6452b05d", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-based inquiry"}], "description": "Students practice foundational skills that support assessment and referral."}, {"id": "2f7ca8d0-bf7a-4573-ad5a-1942f061caa3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Therapeutic boundaries", "children": [{"id": "47b65eb1-16eb-4746-bd0c-1300ebcbccfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality basics"}, {"id": "90bb9614-9663-44d5-9262-a886a566cb34", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional boundaries"}, {"id": "8cb693ad-d976-44d0-b222-bb6cc6d85d1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Dual relationships"}, {"id": "20d53a6a-733d-4bf1-9eeb-afc1db59c001", "type": "concept", "title": "Use of supervision"}], "description": "Good helping relationships require limits that protect clients and practitioners."}]}, {"id": "bf3a80b3-d78b-489b-bc43-5208ba101907", "type": "topic", "title": "Screening, Biopsychosocial Assessment, and Case Formulation", "description": "Connect screening and biopsychosocial assessment to strengths-based case formulation.", "children": [{"id": "868a0942-ffb9-46db-9c4b-81434463cee6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Screening tools and uses", "children": [{"id": "dd76d20b-8d