 and risks of labels"}], "description": "Students learn why diagnostic systems exist and how they are used in services, billing, communication, and research."}, {"id": "307dad05-a1e8-4535-bdf8-7efaa150d270", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using diagnosis carefully", "children": [{"id": "8a573e77-4516-4f28-ac70-a6718d3217b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Symptoms versus diagnoses"}, {"id": "ce624631-1a70-4206-ad8a-ba4a35661eb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical significance and impairment"}, {"id": "de18954a-406d-4560-a7c5-b6e51ceab028", "type": "concept", "title": "Provisional thinking"}, {"id": "10ecebbf-ac37-41bf-9f1c-ba5262b39e21", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral and supervision"}], "description": "The goal is diagnostic literacy, not overconfidence. Students learn to distinguish undergraduate familiarity from licensed diagnostic authority."}, {"id": "93c9a8d1-5299-41ab-b3d0-0079a4bfa822", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Limits and critiques", "children": [{"id": "b6b00c2d-2d77-4821-9c0e-a91a8071daf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural formulation"}, {"id": "f5dac5d3-c059-4c64-8366-bdb7972a68a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicalization concerns"}, {"id": "0899c113-df3a-469c-afb4-1ef793abc801", "type": "concept", "title": "Social suffering and structural conditions"}, {"id": "b807afda-3858-427b-b1cd-5556cf7247db", "type": "concept", "title": "Client voice and meaning"}], "description": "Diagnosis should be used with awareness of culture, power, and context."}]}, {"id": "15b0e639-11a5-4eb6-b34b-3ad423100367", "type": "topic", "title": "Engagement, Helping Relationships, and Basic Interviewing", "description": "Practice respectful engagement, rapport, interviewing, and client-centered communication.", "children": [{"id": "1280417f-5bd4-4b86-8b18-1785ae14f4d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement and rapport", "children": [{"id": "2b8c0846-70ac-46c2-80d6-72acdfb69ef1", "type": "concept", "title": "Warmth and empathy"}, {"id": "13dff9e6-d61e-40bc-